---
title: One Pot Chicken Cilantro Lime Rice
description: Crispy seared bone-in chicken thighs cooked over fragrant jasmine rice finished with fresh lime juice and cilantro, all in one pot.
course: main
cuisine: Mexican
servings: 4
time required: 45 minutes
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 35 minutes
source: https://kitchenswagger.com/One-Pot-Chicken-Cilantro-Lime-Rice-Recipe/
image: https://kitchenswagger.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/cilantro-lime-chicken-and-rice2.jpg
tags:
  - chicken
  - rice
  - one pot
  - weeknight
---

Pat @chicken thighs{4-6}(skin-on, bone-in) dry and season generously with @salt and @pepper. Add @vegetable oil{2-3%tbsp} to a cold #Dutch oven{} and swirl to coat. Place chicken skin-side down, then turn heat to medium.

Cook undisturbed until the skin is golden and releases easily, ~{8-10%minutes}. Flip and cook another ~{3-5%minutes}. Move the chicken to a plate and let the pot cool off the heat for ~{2-3%minutes}, discarding some excess oil if desired.

Return the pot to low heat, melt @butter{2%tbsp}, and add @garlic{4%cloves}(finely chopped), cooking about ~{1%minute}. Stir in @jasmine rice{2%cups}(rinsed) to coat, then season with @salt and @pepper.

Pour in @water{3%cups} and stir. Nestle the chicken back in skin-side up. Raise heat to medium and bring to a simmer. Once bubbling, cover, lower the heat, and cook ~{25%minutes}. Remove from heat and rest ~{10%minutes} with the lid on.

Take out the chicken, then stir @lime juice{2%limes} and @cilantro{1/3%cup}(finely chopped) into the rice with a fork. Serve with the chicken.
